      "id": 2,
      "text": "General George Washington’s army camped twice on the hills behind Bound Brook, where he allegedly unfurled the first Stars and Stripes in 1777.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Bound-Brook",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Battle of Bound Brook, fought on April 13, 1777, was a defeat for the Continental Army, whose forces were routed by roughly 4,000 British troops during the New York and New Jersey campaign.",
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bound_Brook%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "On April 22, 1921, a faulty valve at a Bound Brook paint factory released a cloud of phosgene gas—the same chemical weapon used in World War I—injuring over 100 residents and killing one.",
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bound_Brook%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town’s Historical Commission meets monthly to preserve Bound Brook’s heritage.",
